/* .tablewrap table{min-width:600px} (the desktop side-scroll floor) still applied here,
   so the table stayed pinned to 600px wide even after its rows were switched to this
   stacked block/flex layout — the value half of every row was forced onto one flex line
   at a 600px-wide measure and then hard-clipped by the wrapper at the real ~390px
   viewport, with no scroll affordance a reader would find. Stacked rows don't need the
   600px floor; they need to be exactly as wide as the viewport so long values wrap. */
.tablewrap .dgo-table{min-width:0}
.dgo-table td{min-width:0;overflow-wrap:break-word}}
